  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "When a wolf group grows stronger and larger, neighbouring beast groups lose living space. Migrations influence other beast groups in turn, and the tangled pressure can widen until mixed beast tides form.",
      "chapters": [
        93
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Clansmen on Qing Mao Mountain speak of many wild beast groups ahead that need support during such a small beast tide.",
      "chapters": [
        94
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_qing_mao_mountain"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Old or injured lightning wolves expelled from a pack may rush surrounding beast groups; under mutual influence those rushes help form a small beast horde.",
      "chapters": [
        96
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "As long as a beast group is large enough, a Beast King forms within it. A wild boar group has a wild boar king; a monkey group has a monkey king. The bigger the group, the stronger the king that can rule it.",
      "chapters": [
        114
      ],
